nt-family:Times New Roman;transform-origin:top left;font-kerning:none;min-width:4.86108878960282%;word-break:keep-all;display:inline-flex;justify-content:flex-start;">(13)</span><div style="display:inline;"><span style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:9pt;font-family:Times New Roman;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">Mr. Stemple has sole voting and investment power over 69,070 shares and shared investment and voting power over 2,500 shares.</span></div></div><div class="item-list-element-wrapper" style="margin-left:6.667%;display:flex;margin-top:6pt;justify-content:flex-start;align-items:baseline;margin-bottom:0;margin-right:6.667%;min-width:4.537%;text-align:justify;"><span style="transform:scale(0.67);color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;vertical-align:super;font-size:9pt;font-family:Times New Roman;transform-origin:top left;font-kerning:none;min-width:4.86108878960282%;word-break:keep-all;display:inline-flex;justify-content:flex-start;">(14)</span><div style="display:inline;"><span style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:9pt;font-family:Times New Roman;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">Mr. Bigham has sole voting and investment power over 6,000 shares and holds 5 shares in Pathfinder Bank's ESOP plan.</span></div></div><div class="item-list-element-wrapper" style="margin-left:6.667%;display:flex;margin-top:6pt;justify-content:flex-start;align-items:baseline;margin-bottom:0;margin-right:6.667%;min-width:4.537%;text-align:justify;"><span style="transform:scale(0.67);color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;vertical-align:super;font-size:9pt;font-family:Times New Roman;transform-origin:top left;font-kerning:none;min-width:4.86108878960282%;word-break:keep-all;display:inline-flex;justify-content:flex-start;">(15)</span><div style="display:inline;"><span style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:9pt;font-family:Times New Roman;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">Mr. Butkowski's shares include 14,291 shares in Pathfinder Bank's 401(k) plan, 6,500 shares in an IRA and 6,346 shares in Pathfinder Bank's ESOP. </span></div></div><div class="item-list-element-wrapper" style="margin-left:6.667%;display:flex;margin-top:6pt;justify-content:flex-start;align-items:baseline;margin-bottom:0;margin-right:6.667%;min-width:4.537%;text-align:justify;"><span style="transform:scale(0.67);color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;vertical-align:super;font-size:9pt;font-family:Times New Roman;transform-origin:top left;font-kerning:none;min-width:4.86108878960282%;word-break:keep-all;display:inline-flex;justify-content:flex-start;">(16)</span><div style="display:inline;"><span style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:9pt;font-family:Times New Roman;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">Mr. Dowd&#8217;s shares include 18,052 shares in Pathfinder Bank&#8217;s 401(k) plan and 21,193 shares in Pathfinder Bank&#8217;s ESOP. </span></div></div><div class="item-list-element-wrapper" style="margin-left:6.667%;display:flex;margin-top:6pt;justify-content:flex-start;align-items:baseline;margin-bottom:0;margin-right:6.667%;min-width:4.537%;text-align:justify;"><span style="transform:scale(0.67);color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;vertical-align:super;font-size:9pt;font-family:Times New Roman;transform-origin:top left;font-kerning:none;min-width:4.86108878960282%;word-break:keep-all;display:inline-flex;justify-content:flex-start;">(17)</span><div style="display:inline;"><span style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:9pt;font-family:Times New Roman;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">Mr. McManus's shares include 5,026 shares in Pathfinder Bank's ESOP plan.</span></div></div><div class="item-list-element-wrapper" style="margin-left:6.667%;display:flex;margin-top:6pt;justify-content:flex-start;align-items:baseline;margin-bottom:0;margin-right:6.667%;min-width:4.537%;text-align:justify;"><span style="transform:scale(0.67);color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;vertical-align:super;font-size:9pt;font-family:Times New Roman;transform-origin:top left;font-kerning:none;min-width:4.86108878960282%;word-break:keep-all;display:inline-flex;justify-content:flex-start;">(18)</span><div style="display:inline;"><span style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:9pt;font-family:Times New Roman;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">Mr. O&#8217;Brien&#8217;s shares include 3,255 shares in Pathfinder Bank&#8217;s 401(k) plan and 9,243 shares in Pathfinder Bank&#8217;s ESOP.</span></div></div><div class="item-list-element-wrapper" style="margin-left:6.667%;display:flex;margin-top:6pt;justify-content:flex-start;align-items:baseline;margin-bottom:0;margin-right:6.667%;min-width:4.537%;text-align:justify;"><span style="transform:scale(0.67);color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;vertical-align:super;font-size:9pt;font-family:Times New Roman;transform-origin:top left;font-kerning:none;min-width:4.86108878960282%;word-break:keep-all;display:inline-flex;justify-content:flex-start;">(19)</span><div style="display:inline;"><span style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:9pt;font-family:Times New Roman;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">Mr. Serbun has sole voting and investment power over 4,000 shares and holds 4 shares in Pathfinder Bank's ESOP plan.</span></div></div><div class="item-list-element-wrapper" style="margin-left:6.667%;display:flex;margin-top:6pt;justify-content:flex-start;align-items:baseline;margin-bottom:0;margin-right:6.667%;min-width:4.537%;text-align:justify;"><span style="transform:scale(0.67);color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;vertical-align:super;font-size:9pt;font-family:Times New Roman;transform-origin:top left;font-kerning:none;min-width:4.86108878960282%;word-break:keep-all;display:inline-flex;justify-content:flex-start;">(20)</span><div style="display:inline;"><span style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:9pt;font-family:Times New Roman;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">Mr. Tascarella&#8217;s shares include 15,352 shares in Pathfinder Bank&#8217;s 401(k) plan and 4,392 shares in Pathfinder Bank&#8217;s ESOP.</span></div></div><p style="margin-left:10.667%;font-size:10pt;margin-top:0;font-family:Times New Roman;margin-bottom:0;text-align:justify;"><span style="white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:9pt;font-family:Times New Roman;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">&#160;</span></p><div class="item-list-element-wrapper" style="margin-left:4.667%;display:flex;margin-top:0;justify-content:flex-start;align-items:baseline;margin-bottom:0;min-width:4%;text-align:left;"><span style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-weight:bold;font-size:10pt;font-family:Times New Roman;font-kerning:none;min-width:4.1958188664995335%;word-break:keep-all;display:inline-flex;justify-content:flex-start;">D.</span><div style="display:inline;" id="delinquent"><span style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-weight:bold;font-size:10pt;font-family:Times New Roman;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">DELINQUENT S</span><span style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-weight:bold;font-size:10pt;font-family:Times New Roman;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">ECTION 16(a) REPORTS</span></div></div><p style="margin-left:3.333%;text-indent:-3.448%;padding-left:3.333%;font-size:10pt;margin-top:0;font-family:Times New Roman;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left;"><span style="white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:10pt;font-family:Times New Roman;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">&#160;</span></p><p style="margin-left:8.667%;font-size:10pt;margin-top:0;font-family:Times New Roman;margin-bottom:0;text-align:justify;"><span style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:10pt;font-family:Times New Roman;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">Section 16(a) of the Exchange Act requires the Company&#8217;s directors and Section 16 officers, and persons who own more than 10% of the Company&#8217;s common stock (&#8220;10% beneficial owners&#8221;), to file with the SEC initial reports of ownership and reports of changes in beneficial ownership of the Company&#8217;s common stock. To the Company&#8217;s knowledge, based upon the reports filed and written representations regarding reports required during the 2025 fiscal year, no executive officer or director of the Company failed to file reports required by Section 16(a) on a timely basis.</span></p><p style="margin-left:3.333%;text-indent:-3.448%;padding-left:3.333%;font-size:10pt;margin-top:0;font-family:Times New Roman;margin-bottom:0;text-align:justify;"><span style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:10pt;font-family:Times New Roman;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;"> </span></p><div class="item-list-element-wrapper" style="margin-left:4.667%;display:flex;margin-top:0;justify-content:flex-start;align-items:baseline;margin-bottom:0;min-width:4%;text-align:left;"><span style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-weight:bold;font-size:10pt;font-family:Times New Roman;font-kerning:none;min-width:4.1958188664995335%;word-break:keep-all;display:inline-flex;justify-content:flex-start;">E.</span><div style="display:inline;" id="transactions"><span style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-weight:bold;font-size:10pt;font-family:Times New Roman;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">TRANSACTIONS WITH CERTAIN RELATED PERSONS</span></div></div><p style="font-size:10pt;margin-top:0;font-family:Times New Roman;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left;"><span style="white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:10pt;font-family:Times New Roman;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">&#160;</span></p><p style="margin-left:8.667%;font-size:10pt;margin-top:0;font-family:Times New Roman;margin-bottom:0;text-align:justify;"><span style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:10pt;font-family:Times New Roman;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">The Sarbanes-Oxley Act of 2002 generally prohibits an issuer from (i) extending or maintaining credit; (ii) arranging for the extension of credit; or (iii) renewing an extension of credit in the form of a personal loan for an officer or director. There are several exceptions to this general prohibition, however, one of which is applicable to us. This prohibition does not apply to loans made by a depository institution that is insured by the FDIC and is subject to the insider lending restrictions of the Federal Reserve Act. Regulations permit executive officers and directors to receive the same loan terms through programs that are widely available to other employees, as long as the executive officer or director is not given preferential treatment compared to the other participating employees. The Bank currently has loans to each of the following executive officers and/or directors or their immediate families: Eric Allyn, Robert Butkowski, Meghan Crawford-Hamlin, James Dowd, John Funiciello, Joseph McManus, William O&#8217;Brien, John Sharkey III, Lloyd "Buddy" Stemple and Ronald G. Tascarella.</span></p><p style="margin-left:8.667%;font-size:10pt;margin-top:0;font-family:Times New Roman;margin-bottom:0;text-align:justify;"><span style="white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:10pt;font-family:Times New Roman;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">&#160;</span></p><p style="margin-left:8.667%;font-size:10pt;margin-top:0;font-family:Times New Roman;margin-bottom:0;text-align:justify;"><span style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:10pt;font-family:Times New Roman;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">After one year of service at the Bank, full-time employees and directors are entitled to receive a primary residence mortgage loan at an interest rate of 0.25% below market, consistent with applicable laws and regulations. Until 2021, the rate was at 0.50% below market.</span><span style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:10pt;font-family:Times New Roman;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;"> </span></p><p style="margin-left:8.667%;font-size:10pt;margin-top:0;font-family:Times New Roman;margin-bottom:0;text-align:justify;"><span style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:10pt;font-family:Times New Roman;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;"> </span></p><p style="margin-left:8.667%;font-size:10pt;margin-top:0;font-family:Times New Roman;margin-bottom:0;text-align:justify;"><span style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:10pt;font-family:Times New Roman;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">The chart below lists the executive officers and directors who participated in the employee mortgage loan program during the years ended December 31, 2025 and 2024 and certain information with respect to their loans. No other directors or executive officers participated in the employee mortgage loan program during the years ended December 31, 2025 and 2024.</span></p><p style="margin-left:6.667%;font-size:10pt;margin-top:0;font-family:Times New Roman;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left;"><span style="white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:9pt;font-family:Times New Roman;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">&#160;</span></p>
